ce gains of sparse convolution.'], 'type': ['generic', 'GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4, 5]}, 'Sparse convolution': {'description': ['A type of convolution that utilizes sparsity to reduce computational requirements and improve classification speed.', 'Convolution operations performed on sparse data, aiming to reduce computational complexity.', 'A convolution operation optimized for sparse weight tensors, aiming to reduce computational cost and accelerate CNNs.', 'The constraints and drawbacks associated with sparse convolution, including inapplicability to small kernel sizes, which limits its potential.'], 'type': ['generic', 'method', 'GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4, 5]}, '2,371 images per second': {'description': ['The AlexNet classification throughput achieved by the optimized sparse CNN implementation.', 'The performance metric used to measure classification speed, representing the number of images processed per second.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 6]}, '1,120 images per second': {'description': ['The AlexNet classification throughput achieved by the optimized sparse CNN implementation.', 'The performance metric used to measure classification speed, representing the number of images processed per second.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 6]}, 'SpMDM (sparse matrix and dense matrix multiplication)': {'description': ['A method for performing matrix multiplication with sparse matrices, often used in fully connected layers.', 'A technique used to implement fully connected layers, leveraging sparse matrix multiplication to exploit sparsity.'], 'type': ['method', 'GENERIC'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 5]}, 'Images per second': {'description': ['A performance metric used to evaluate the speed of CNNs, specifically the number of images processed per second.', 'A performance metric used to quantify the classification speed of CNNs, representing the number of images processed per second.', 'The performance metric used